# Visual brainstorming companion (local mockups)
.superpowers/

# The test-run artefacts this repo's own working notes tell you to create:
# `pytest ... > run.log 2>&1; echo "PYTEST_EXIT=$?" > run.exit`. The exit code
# has to be captured to its own file because a pipeline's status is the LAST
# command's, so a `| tail` turns a usage error green -- which is why the recipe
# exists and why its output is a normal part of working here rather than a
# stray file. Two phases on a shared machine, hence the numbered second pair.
run.log
run.exit
run2.log
run2.exit

# The nine review and handover drafts in the root. The migration plan's
# appendix C excludes them: their fate is decided separately and they do not
# enter the repository as part of that programme. Listed here because relying
# on them merely being untracked did not hold -- a `git add -A` swept them in
# twice on 2026-08-27, and the second time only because the first was already
# being cleaned up. Ignoring them makes the exclusion mechanical instead of a
# thing someone has to remember; it does not decide their fate, and they stay
# on disk exactly as appendix C describes.
/CODE_REVIEW_REPORT.md
/HANDOVER.md
/NEXT_SESSION_PROMPT.md
/PROPOSAL_BAYESMITH.md
/PROPOSAL_MERGED.md
/PROPOSAL_RHEPLICANT.md
/PROPOSAL_bayesmith_bayesian.md
/PROPOSAL_rheplicant_nonbayesian.md
/REVIEW_REPORT.md
